 "notes": {
  "n-flow": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -420,
   "w": 1800,
   "page": "flow",
   "text": "The installer’s screens, a proposal (spec installer 001, decision 0014). This page: the Note Air from a Chromium browser, start to installed, in order. The PC page has the same screens with the PC’s texts (SC-005); every device or system name comes from data/fixtures.js, as from a device description. Buttons link to the next board. White first; every board takes the voice, scheme and pen pickers. Parts Interleaf lacks (stepper, primary button, progress, step list, choice row, field) are drawn in installer.css on Interleaf tokens."
  },
  "t-flow": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -200,
   "page": "flow",
   "kind": "title1",
   "text": "Flow · Note Air"
  },
  "t-pc": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -200,
   "page": "pc",
   "kind": "title1",
   "text": "Flow · UEFI PC"
  },
  "n-pc": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -420,
   "w": 1800,
   "page": "pc",
   "text": "The same screens for a PC started from the GlassineOS USB stick. Reaching the machine is one screen with nothing to connect. Verify runs on GlassineOS’s first start, because the live session ends with the restart (a design question)."
  },
  "t-states": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -200,
   "page": "states",
   "kind": "title1",
   "text": "Variants and failures"
  },
  "t-again": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -200,
   "page": "again",
   "kind": "title1",
   "text": "Cut off · already installed · back to stock"
  },
  "t-parts": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -200,
   "page": "parts",
   "kind": "title1",
   "text": "Parts"
  },
  "n-supply": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": 15900,
   "w": 1800,
   "page": "states",
   "text": "A file only the person can provide (installer spec 004): the emergency programmer for the backup. The installer names what it must match and the name it is usually found under, to copy; it links to no site and opens no search. It checks the file’s checksum against the known ones from the device description, and the chip and key; an unknown file is sent only after the person ticks the warning. Every text comes from data/fixtures.js (the description’s [[supplied_files]] and texts), so another device or route uses the same screens."
  }
 }
}
